IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ltcs-seat-owner-driver`

-- Motor Accidents (Lifetime Care and Support) Act 2006 (NSW) -- worked cases for the two exported questions in
-- ltcs-seat-owner-driver.l4 (s 54, the seat of the owner or driver, or other person at fault). Every expected value was
-- worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about
-- the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Amounts are illustrative. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as
-- advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `owner and driver cases`

`owner driving` MEANS `I owned the vehicle and was driving it`
`owner not driving` MEANS `I owned the vehicle and someone else was driving it`
`driver` MEANS `I was driving the vehicle and someone else owned it`
`other at fault` MEANS `I was partly at fault but was not the owner or driver of a motor vehicle`

§§ `s 54(1), (3), (5)-(9), (11) -- can the Authority recover from me`

-- Arguments: my part, fault of owner or driver, no third-party policy, interstate or Commonwealth scheme, Chapter 3
-- applies, not required to be registered or insured, participant bought in under s 7A, owner's defence, driver's defence.
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the participant's care costs from me` `owner driving` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A third-party policy was in force: s 54(1)(b) fails.
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the participant's care costs from me` `owner driving` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not the owner's or driver's fault: s 54(1)(a) fails.
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the participant's care costs from me` `owner driving` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Interstate or Commonwealth scheme: the insurer is the appropriate person (s 54(5)(b)).
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the participant's care costs from me` `owner driving` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 54(6), (9), (11).
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the participant's care costs from me` `owner driving` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the participant's care costs from me` `owner driving` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the participant's care costs from me` `owner driving` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 54(7): the owner's defence, proved and not proved.
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the participant's care costs from me` `owner not driving` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the participant's care costs from me` `owner not driving` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The owner's defence needs someone else driving: no help to an owner who drove.
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the participant's care costs from me` `owner driving` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 54(8): the driver's defence, proved and not proved.
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the participant's care costs from me` `driver` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the participant's care costs from me` `driver` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 54(3), read apart from s 54(1) (fork F9): an insured vehicle and no driver fault do not matter.
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the participant's care costs from me` `other at fault` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the participant's care costs from me` `other at fault` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the participant's care costs from me` `other at fault` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Authority recover the participant's care costs from me` `none of these` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 54(2), (3), (4) -- how much`

-- Paid $400,000; future present value $1,600,000; the present value of the liabilities is $2,000,000.
-- Arguments as above, then paid, future, the participant's share (contributory negligence), my share (s 54(3)).
#ASSERT `How much can the Authority recover from me` `owner driving` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 400000 1600000 0 0 EQUALS JUST 2000000
-- 25 per cent contributory negligence: $1,500,000.
#ASSERT `How much can the Authority recover from me` `owner driving` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 400000 1600000 25 0 EQUALS JUST 1500000
#ASSERT `How much can the Authority recover from me` `driver` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 400000 1600000 100 0 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `How much can the Authority recover from me` `owner driving` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 400000 1600000 101 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `How much can the Authority recover from me` `owner driving` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 400000 1600000 (0 MINUS 1) 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Another person 30 per cent responsible: $600,000; the participant's 20 per cent is not taken off again (fork F10).
#ASSERT `How much can the Authority recover from me` `other at fault` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 400000 1600000 20 30 EQUALS JUST 600000
#ASSERT `How much can the Authority recover from me` `other at fault` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 400000 1600000 20 101 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `How much can the Authority recover from me` `other at fault` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 400000 1600000 20 100 EQUALS JUST 2000000
-- Insured vehicle: nothing recoverable from the owner.
#ASSERT `How much can the Authority recover from me` `owner driving` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 400000 1600000 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- The participant bought in under s 7A: nothing (s 54(11)).
#ASSERT `How much can the Authority recover from me` `other at fault` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 400000 1600000 0 50 EQUALS JUST 0
